# pointdelete

- Label: Point Delete
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 1 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pointdelete.html
- Summary (EN): The Point Delete node removes selected points from a point cloud and always outputs a point cloud. Primitives on the input are not passed through.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Point Delete supprime des points selon un attribut entier et renvoie toujours un nuage de points, les primitives étant perdues.

- Inputs meaning: ["points: original points; the output is a subset of these", "dead (optional): integer attribute marking points to delete; must match the point count of the first input; zero keeps the point"]

- Key parameters: ["Delete Attribute: integer point attribute deciding removal; zero keeps the point, any other value removes it"]

- Caveats: ["Primitives on the input are dropped; only point data survives.", "The dead input must match the first input's point count.", "Available since Houdini 22.0."]

